{"t":1786257424574,"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b3b88c73a111c95b442dd97353457ab9a68db64.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-100.2,45.69],[-100.16,45.81],[-99.65,45.83],[-99.62,45.59],[-99.68,45.5],[-100.2,45.69]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b3b88c73a111c95b442dd97353457ab9a68db64.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b3b88c73a111c95b442dd97353457ab9a68db64.001.1","areaDesc":"Campbell, SD; Edmunds, SD; McPherson, SD; Walworth, SD","geocode":{"SAME":["046021","046045","046089","046129"],"UGC":["SDC021","SDC045","SDC089","SDC129"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/SDC021","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/SDC045","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/SDC089","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/SDC129"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-09T01:27:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-09T01:27:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-09T01:27:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-09T02:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-09T02:15:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Aberdeen SD","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 9 at 1:27AM CDT until August 9 at 2:15AM CDT by NWS Aberdeen SD","description":"SVRABR\n\nThe National Weather Service in Aberdeen has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nSoutheastern Campbell County in north central South Dakota...\nNorthwestern Edmunds County in north central South Dakota...\nSouthwestern McPherson County in north central South Dakota...\nNortheastern Walworth County in north central South Dakota...\n\n* Until 215 AM CDT.\n\n* At 127 AM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Mound City,\nor 7 miles south of Herreid, moving east at 25 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Ping pong ball size hail and 60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect hail\ndamage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect\nwind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nMound City.","instruction":"Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from\nwindows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds and large\nhail.\n\nTorrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to\nflash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.","response":"Shelter","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SVRABR"],"WMOidentifier":["WUUS53 KABR 090627"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-09T06:26:00-00:00...storm...277DEG...21KT...45.74,-100.09"],"windThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxWindGust":["60 MPH"],"hailThreat":["RADAR INDICATED"],"maxHailSize":["1.50"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KABR.SV.W.0197.260809T0627Z-260809T0715Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-09T02:15:00-05:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SVR"],"NationalWeatherService":["SVW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7e5fc424cf17d33594c9e8732f4a6e0710b93af2.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-98.8,28.17],[-98.59,28.36],[-98.33,28.45],[-98.33,28.33],[-98.54,28.26],[-98.8,28.07],[-98.8,28.17]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7e5fc424cf17d33594c9e8732f4a6e0710b93af2.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7e5fc424cf17d33594c9e8732f4a6e0710b93af2.001.1","areaDesc":"McMullen, TX","geocode":{"SAME":["048311"],"UGC":["TXC311"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/TXC311"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.02aa56307f6319b87aaa3f9fb059fedf8cb7b3e5.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.02aa56307f6319b87aaa3f9fb059fedf8cb7b3e5.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-08T08:45:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-08T20:13:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-08T20:13:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-08T20:13:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-09T11:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-09T15:35:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Corpus Christi TX","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 8 at 8:13PM CDT until August 9 at 3:35PM CDT by NWS Corpus Christi TX","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Texas...\n\nNueces River Near Tilden affecting McMullen County.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.\n\n* WHERE...Nueces River near Tilden.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 14.0 feet, Minor lowland flooding occurs, and causes\nsloughs and peripheral channels near the main stream to cut off\nareas of the flood plain, isolating livestock and damaging\nequipment in low areas. Oil field tank batteries and pump jacks\nflood.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 PM CDT Saturday the stage was 14.3 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 11.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage\ntonight and fall below action stage by late Monday.\n- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 14.3\nfeet on 05/24/2004.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 090113"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL SUNDAY AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0026.000000T0000Z-260809T2035Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-09T15:35:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4012e8981516f4acc66aaf3deb0be40ca8d1a929.001.1,2026-08-07T20:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a4006eb38dda81396de878a3ee30877db05dc184.001.1,2026-08-07T08:43:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.422f915b9c8698a61ceeecbb773519636c1559f0.001.1,2026-08-06T20:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c086fb0cb122a2dcaad2d633e16163ca1e2f740.002.1,2026-08-06T08:31:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd351168adba7b138d4b2fd5b257e34ba80d69c4.002.1,2026-08-05T19:53:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15a54361c4ea7596611f53154fbe235d68afe15a.002.1,2026-08-05T10:56:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.002.1,2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0d85f3f3b48cc9017f55a16e1f1acf4cc74e9f0b.002.1,2026-08-04T15:51:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52c53adf21b8a3c6773f1bc49de7351006f6e777.002.1,2026-08-04T08:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1890e16dec93bc7bd2c40c556f7d88b51dfba240.002.1,2026-08-03T20:13:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c2d46f696ba508a8268a87165a57be61f4e50bb.002.1,2026-08-03T09:17:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a89341f8395f18ac2219ce1a412989c19cd5d270.002.1,2026-08-02T20:24:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.135a0f1988967